        <detaileddescription>
<para>calculates &apos;hydraulic conductivity&apos;</para>
<para>the hydraulic conductivity of element i is calculated from the permeability of the element and the average of the nodal fluid viscosities. This conductivity is multiplied with the nodal fluid density average since the goal is to calculate the mass flux.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>If the property has the value of &apos;where&apos;, it is changed to the value of &apos;to&apos; </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
